WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.358
Insidious Chapter Three brings back the ghost hunter hero Elise Rainier, and

00:00:03.364 --> 00:00:06.286
we learn more about her backstory, what happened to her husband, and we meet

00:00:06.308 --> 00:00:07.322
her dog, Warren.

00:00:07.386 --> 00:00:08.186
-[Elise] It's okay, Warren.

00:00:08.218 --> 00:00:08.970
-[Elise] Go upstairs.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.914
In my previous Insidious analysis videos, I've discussed the connections

00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:14.394
between the Insidious franchise and the Conjuring franchise.

00:00:14.442 --> 00:00:17.886
From camerawork to Easter eggs to character names, Elise is basically the

00:00:17.908 --> 00:00:20.762
Insidious equivalent of the psychic Lorraine Warren from the Conjuring.

00:00:20.826 --> 00:00:23.902
So I think her dog was given the name Warren in honor of Lorraine, since

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.722
they already used the name Lorraine for a different Insidious character.

00:00:26.786 --> 00:00:29.894
To learn about all of the movie secrets, stick around to the end of this video. 

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:36.355
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:37.906
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:00:37.938 --> 00:00:40.646
The third chapter of the Insidious franchise takes us back before the

00:00:40.668 --> 00:00:43.606
original, where a then retired Elise is approached by Quinn Brenner, who

00:00:43.628 --> 00:00:46.934
wants to contact her deceased mother, but accidentally reaches something far

00:00:46.972 --> 00:00:48.642
more... Unsidious.

00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:52.158
James Wan, the director of Insidious One and Two, was busy making a

00:00:52.164 --> 00:00:52.906
Fast and Furious sequel.

00:00:52.938 --> 00:00:56.122
So the screenwriter Leigh Whannel got the call up to direct

00:00:56.186 --> 00:00:57.182
his first feature film.

00:00:57.236 --> 00:00:58.174
Side story, I love chapter three.

00:00:58.212 --> 00:01:00.766
And when I was taking my notes for this episode, I was thinking about how

00:01:00.788 --> 00:01:02.190
I've seen this movie so many times.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.210
This scene where Quinn hears noises in the night isn't going to be as scary.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.798
She hears someone moving around in the vacant apartment upstairs.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.154
And right as that happened, I heard someone walking around upstairs from me,

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:14.194
which was slightly creepy, and it distracted me enough to where I actually

00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:15.890
got jump scared by the bell.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.266
And apparently, I was not the only one who experienced something unexpected

00:01:21.298 --> 00:01:22.386
with this scene.

00:01:22.578 --> 00:01:26.418
-[Stefanie] There's a scene with a bell that's supposed to wake me up, and we rehearsed

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:30.406
-[Stefanie] it a few times, and by the time we shot it for the first time, he puts this

00:01:30.428 --> 00:01:31.126
-[Stefanie] air horn on.

00:01:31.148 --> 00:01:32.860
-[Stefanie] It scared me so bad.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.138
-[Stefanie] I mean, I guess he got the reaction he wanted.

00:01:36.224 --> 00:01:38.966
I always find it cool when the director finds a way to get real reactions

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:39.702
from the actors.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:43.120
Anyway, I've got some things you might have missed, so let's get into them.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.306
(Air Horn)

00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:49.816
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.694
Quinn's room is filled with decorations, some of which are the high school

00:01:53.732 --> 00:01:55.834
play she's been in and also a lot of band merch.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.114
Her favorites seem to be Pixies.

00:01:57.162 --> 00:02:00.046
She wears a Pixie's shirt, has two stickers on her door and one on her

00:02:00.068 --> 00:02:01.546
bookcase. The other is The Cure.

00:02:01.578 --> 00:02:03.902
There are two stickers on her door and a poster on her wall.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.726
I wondered if her interest in these bands could be because of her mom, who

00:02:06.748 --> 00:02:08.950
is stated to have loved vinyl records and old music.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.054
This is kind of confirmed in a deleted scene where Quinn and her friend find

00:02:12.092 --> 00:02:14.646
her dad's memory box that includes all of his keepsakes from his

00:02:14.668 --> 00:02:18.034
relationship with her mom, including a ticket to see The Cure from 1980.

00:02:18.082 --> 00:02:21.366
The scene may also explain why Quinn is interested in pursuing theater and

00:02:21.388 --> 00:02:23.210
why her dad is afraid of letting her go.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.534
This note explains that Quinn's mom once traveled away to pursue her dreams,

00:02:26.582 --> 00:02:29.754
and it was hard on her dad, which would give additional context to this line. 

00:02:29.792 --> 00:02:34.186
-[Sean] I see her every single day when I look at you.

00:02:34.288 --> 00:02:37.278
All of these little details show how important Quinn's mom was to her and

00:02:37.284 --> 00:02:40.414
help make the ending, where her spirit helps save her daughter even more impactful.

00:02:40.452 --> 00:02:43.726
I also found it interesting that in the Further, Quinn's room is

00:02:43.748 --> 00:02:45.354
completely barren and undecorated.

00:02:45.402 --> 00:02:48.286
Maybe a sign that the entity that she's been encountering to that point was

00:02:48.308 --> 00:02:48.922
not her mother.

00:02:48.986 --> 00:02:52.238
The lines that Quinn is rehearsing for her audition say you'll go to the end

00:02:52.244 --> 00:02:53.854
of the world and you'll find me waiting there.

00:02:53.892 --> 00:02:56.838
You gave me life when I was dying, when I was leaving this world.

00:02:56.924 --> 00:03:00.086
This describes how Lily rescued Quinn from having her soul taken by the

00:03:00.108 --> 00:03:01.382
Man Who Can't Breathe at the end.

00:03:01.436 --> 00:03:04.002
The play is called Separated by Lights by Bailey Conway.

00:03:04.066 --> 00:03:07.186
In Insidious, the real world is sometimes referred to as the light, whereas

00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:09.330
the Further, where Quinn's mom is, is the dark.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.242
Bailey Conway is also the name of one of the film's co-producers.

00:03:12.306 --> 00:03:15.178
Speaking of crew reference Easter Eggs, James Wan has a cameo as the

00:03:15.184 --> 00:03:16.282
director of the theater school.

00:03:16.336 --> 00:03:19.430
Another familiar face is this woman that Elise talks to in the Further.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.746
This is Leigh Whannel's wife, Corbett Tuck, who also played two small parts in

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:23.718
the first Insidious.

00:03:23.814 --> 00:03:26.766
Another tie-in to the previous movies is the return of Specs and Tucker, who

00:03:26.788 --> 00:03:28.842
have their own web series called Spectral Sightings.

00:03:28.906 --> 00:03:30.474
Queen's brother Alex is a fan.

00:03:30.522 --> 00:03:33.870
On his computer monitor, you can see the URL spectralsightings.com.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.302
At the time, this was a real website that you could go to.

00:03:36.356 --> 00:03:38.366
It seems like it was mostly used to promote Insidious: Chapter Two.

00:03:38.398 --> 00:03:41.486
The post contained some field videos with Specs and Tucker,

00:03:41.518 --> 00:03:43.774
and some interviews with Specs, Tucker and Elise.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:46.834
There's nothing substantial here, and the events of the videos, which take

00:03:46.872 --> 00:03:50.166
place before the beginning of chapter one, are rendered non-canon by the

00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:51.238
events of chapter three.

00:03:51.324 --> 00:03:54.678
So it's weird that they decided to highlight the URL in chapter three.

00:03:54.764 --> 00:03:56.982
Not one of the better viral marketing efforts I've seen.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.930
I'm not sure why Alex is such a fan.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.698
-[Alex] Showed him that one where you guys get the ghost out of that one hotel.

00:04:01.794 --> 00:04:03.090
-[Alex] The boiler room ghost.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.038
-[Alex] That was a good one.

00:04:04.124 --> 00:04:07.126
This line could be a reference to The Shining, which features a hotel full

00:04:07.148 --> 00:04:09.574
of ghosts and a very important plot line about the boiler room in the book.

00:04:09.612 --> 00:04:13.006
Leigh and his wife are clearly fans of Stanley Kubrick, the

00:04:13.028 --> 00:04:14.842
director of the film adaptation of The Shining.

00:04:14.906 --> 00:04:18.206
Kubrick also directed an adaptation of A Clockwork Orange, which Quinn can

00:04:18.228 --> 00:04:19.278
be seen reading in bed.

00:04:19.364 --> 00:04:22.462
The reason she ends up bedridden is because she got struck down by a car

00:04:22.516 --> 00:04:24.794
while staring at the Man Who Can't Breathe in the hospital.

00:04:24.842 --> 00:04:29.102
The EKG machine has the date for August 2014, which is obviously a mistake

00:04:29.166 --> 00:04:31.490
because this movie takes place around 2007.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.914
There's a similar mistake on her laptop later on, where the date is July 24, 2014

00:04:34.952 --> 00:04:38.686
but as she's being treated at the emergency room, there's an

00:04:38.718 --> 00:04:39.902
Easter egg in a deleted scene.

00:04:39.966 --> 00:04:42.978
If you look at the doctor's badge, it says Our Lady of the Angels.

00:04:43.074 --> 00:04:46.358
This is the same hospital where Parker Crane attacked Josh Lambert in a

00:04:46.364 --> 00:04:49.350
flashback in Insidious Two. The characters go back there in the present

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.534
during that second film, and it's now abandoned, meaning that it closed down

00:04:52.572 --> 00:04:53.974
shortly after the third chapter.

00:04:54.022 --> 00:04:57.034
Or maybe the hospital that Quinn stays at is a new location that they moved to.

00:04:57.072 --> 00:05:00.054
During her treatment, she slips into the Further and sees the demon,

00:05:00.102 --> 00:05:03.114
suggesting that she has the same traveling ability that Dalton Lambert had.

00:05:03.152 --> 00:05:05.646
There's another character in Quinn's building who also seems to have this ability.

00:05:05.668 --> 00:05:08.766
Her neighbor Grace describes the Man Who Can't Breathe living in

00:05:08.788 --> 00:05:09.466
the vents.

00:05:09.578 --> 00:05:16.094
-[Grace] He's up there right now, standing in your room. You will see him. 

00:05:16.292 --> 00:05:19.962
But her ramblings are treated as a part of her dementia.

00:05:20.026 --> 00:05:23.086
When she passes away, her husband expresses how he tried to tell her how

00:05:23.108 --> 00:05:24.750
much she meant to him before she was gone.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.066
It an important scene because Harry is one of three characters in the movie

00:05:28.098 --> 00:05:29.682
who has to deal with this kind of grief.

00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:32.726
Quinn's main objective in the film is to talk to her mother again, so she

00:05:32.748 --> 00:05:34.822
can say all of the things she never got a chance to say.

00:05:34.876 --> 00:05:37.766
And Elise goes through something similar with her late husband, Jack, who

00:05:37.788 --> 00:05:39.190
she never got to say goodbye to.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:42.258
The message is clear the life that you spend with your loved ones is what's

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:45.386
important, and you can't spend your life in depression, ruminating over your losses.

00:05:45.408 --> 00:05:48.794
At the beginning of the movie, Elise is in retirement, afraid to use

00:05:48.832 --> 00:05:50.598
her gift after what happened to her husband.

00:05:50.694 --> 00:05:53.946
Quinn, after losing her mom and getting disabled by a motorist, has also

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:56.942
fallen into a depression, claiming that she can no longer taste food.

00:05:56.996 --> 00:05:59.962
When Elise sees her in the state and inspires her to come out of retirement

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:03.278
to help the girl. Un this movie, Quinn's depression takes a

00:06:03.284 --> 00:06:03.706
physical form in the Further.

00:06:03.706 --> 00:06:06.954
As the demon slowly takes her soul, we see a deformed version of her appear

00:06:07.002 --> 00:06:07.790
alongside it.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.734
This version of Quinn has no eyes, mouth, hands or feet.

00:06:10.782 --> 00:06:13.986
But as Quinn loses her will to live, the Man Who Can't Breathe absorbs more

00:06:14.008 --> 00:06:14.574
of her soul.

00:06:14.622 --> 00:06:17.662
And this second, Quinn gains more features, like a mouth, and eventually

00:06:17.726 --> 00:06:19.042
hands and everything else.

00:06:19.096 --> 00:06:22.054
It's a good visual representation of how far along she is to being

00:06:22.092 --> 00:06:23.574
possessed, something we don't really have.

00:06:23.612 --> 00:06:26.822
In the first Insidious, it was up to Elise to come out of her shell to save

00:06:26.876 --> 00:06:28.918
Quinn, who still had so much to live for.

00:06:29.004 --> 00:06:30.760
-[Elise] Everybody's going to die one day.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:37.286
-[Elise] I think it is high time for me to get out of my house while I'm still alive.

00:06:37.398 --> 00:06:40.478
And she does all of this despite knowing that if she comes back to the

00:06:40.484 --> 00:06:44.430
Further, there's an even darker presence waiting for her in the shadows.

00:06:44.517 --> 00:06:47.933
(Thunder)

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.135
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:56.606
One evening, Elise slips through her Book of Seeing, and if we go frame by frame,

00:06:56.628 --> 00:07:00.142
you can see stories of some kind of blue fairy and a wicked castle.

00:07:00.206 --> 00:07:01.362
I'm not sure what that's about.

00:07:01.416 --> 00:07:02.654
Probably one of her past cases.

00:07:02.702 --> 00:07:06.110
But what's interesting is this part, scribbled in thick, black crayon.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.138
It says, you should have never come here to the place where I live.

00:07:09.224 --> 00:07:10.582
The dark is going to kill you.

00:07:10.636 --> 00:07:13.874
I have killed many more times, and many children hear screams.

00:07:13.922 --> 00:07:16.694
I would assume that this is something told to Elise by the Bride in Black,

00:07:16.732 --> 00:07:19.526
an antagonist from the first and second Insidious, who would eventually be

00:07:19.548 --> 00:07:20.502
the one to take her life.

00:07:20.556 --> 00:07:23.286
When she visits the Further to try to help Quinn, the elevator takes her

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:24.454
somewhere unfamiliar to her.

00:07:24.492 --> 00:07:26.726
This is the second house that the Lambert family lives in Insidious One.

00:07:26.748 --> 00:07:29.718
The Further is capable of showing different points in

00:07:29.724 --> 00:07:31.758
time, and we're actually looking into the future.

00:07:31.844 --> 00:07:35.118
The Lamberts do not live here yet, but we can see a family photo on top of

00:07:35.124 --> 00:07:35.994
Renai's piano.

00:07:36.042 --> 00:07:39.246
Elise is essentially being shown a premonition of her death, which makes her

00:07:39.268 --> 00:07:42.350
look even more brave in the original movie, because she goes to that house

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.282
knowing that she's most likely going to die.

00:07:44.346 --> 00:07:47.362
As further proof, she comes across this woman, who we've never met before,

00:07:47.416 --> 00:07:50.594
but is listed in the credits as Lambert Woman, who points to the living room and says this.

00:07:50.632 --> 00:07:56.660
-[Lambert Woman] I always wanted to know how I would go.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:01.380
-[Lambert Woman] Tell me friend, how I meet my end.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:06.406
And this is the armchair where Elise would meet her end three years later.

00:08:06.508 --> 00:08:08.994
There are other examples of retroactive foreshadowing.

00:08:09.042 --> 00:08:11.846
The way the Man Who Can't Breathe appears in Quinn's window is similar to

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:13.654
the long haired fiend from the first movie.

00:08:13.702 --> 00:08:16.346
During Carl's lunch with Elise, he gives her some important advice for

00:08:16.368 --> 00:08:17.722
fighting the Bride and Black.

00:08:17.856 --> 00:08:19.980
-[Carl] All right, you're stronger than her.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.030
-[Carl] You're alive.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.286
This would be the same advice that Elise would go on to give Josh during his

00:08:26.308 --> 00:08:27.210
journey into the Further.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:30.314
After this first encounter with the supernatural, Tucker can be seen icing

00:08:30.362 --> 00:08:32.906
his leg, which may call back to Specs nursing his injuries in the first one.

00:08:32.938 --> 00:08:35.806
On the topic of Specs, he finds a way to make himself

00:08:35.838 --> 00:08:36.898
useful to the team.

00:08:36.984 --> 00:08:39.106
-[Elise] What's your contribution?

00:08:39.128 --> 00:08:39.714
-[Tucker] This should be good. 
-[Specs] It's not good.

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:40.434
-[Specs] It's great.

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:41.810
-[Specs] It's our blog.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:43.762
-[Specs] I'm the writer of it.

00:08:43.816 --> 00:08:45.762
It's definitely not that good, as we've seen.

00:08:45.816 --> 00:08:49.038
But it is a fun fourth wall break because Leigh Whannel is literally the writer

00:08:49.054 --> 00:08:50.350
of this trilogy of movies.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.430
Specs and Tucker have their own van, and the license plate looks like this.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.662
There's a double meaning here.

00:08:54.716 --> 00:08:56.834
It reads as Specter, the thing that they're hunting.

00:08:56.882 --> 00:08:59.554
But it also contains both of their names Specs and Tucker.

00:08:59.602 --> 00:09:02.170
There's also a little bit of insight about the technology they use.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.546
Tucker has a wireless display with switches at the bottom labeled Tesla and Gauss. 

00:09:05.568 --> 00:09:07.542
These are both units of measurement.

00:09:07.606 --> 00:09:10.746
Tesla is used to define magnetic flux density, which has something to do

00:09:10.768 --> 00:09:12.134
with electromagnetic fields.

00:09:12.182 --> 00:09:14.794
Paranormal researchers and ghost hunters believe ghosts can generate

00:09:14.842 --> 00:09:17.934
electromagnetic fields of their own, which is why ghosts in movies are often

00:09:17.972 --> 00:09:20.938
associated with flickering lights or malfunctioning electronics.

00:09:21.034 --> 00:09:23.322
Gauss is another unit of magnetic flux density.

00:09:23.386 --> 00:09:26.890
Both are named after scientists Nikola Tesla and Carl Friedrich Gauss.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.730
The movie seems to be telling us that this interpretation is correct,

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.626
because when Quinn starts to be possessed by the Man Who Can't Breathe, we

00:09:32.648 --> 00:09:33.982
see the lights begin to flicker.

00:09:34.046 --> 00:09:37.054
This entity, however, is far more capable than just producing

00:09:37.102 --> 00:09:38.334
electromagnetic fields.

00:09:38.382 --> 00:09:41.286
After Elise is attacked in her reading room, you can spot this tear in her

00:09:41.308 --> 00:09:43.142
sweater as if something is flashed through it.

00:09:43.196 --> 00:09:45.974
In my videos on Insidious One and Two, I discussed how these movies took

00:09:46.012 --> 00:09:47.922
after the first and second Poltergeist films.

00:09:47.986 --> 00:09:48.946
So does Insidious: Chapter Three

00:09:48.978 --> 00:09:49.494
Follow the trend and

00:09:49.532 --> 00:09:52.826
pay homage to Poltergeist Three? Other than the fact

00:09:52.848 --> 00:09:55.978
that both movies take place in a multiunit complex, not really.

00:09:56.064 --> 00:09:56.618
Thank God.

00:09:56.704 --> 00:09:59.846
There is a nice moment in Insidious where Quinn and Alex get too impatient

00:09:59.878 --> 00:10:02.266
waiting for the elevator and opt to take the stairs instead.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:05.274
A nice setup for when Quinn gets captured and trapped on the uninhabited

00:10:05.322 --> 00:10:05.818
fifth floor.

00:10:05.818 --> 00:10:09.034
And due to her wheelchair, the elevator is her only avenue of escape.

00:10:09.082 --> 00:10:11.642
Knowing the elevator is slow really adds to the suspense.

00:10:11.706 --> 00:10:12.634
So that's Insidious: Chapter Three.

00:10:12.682 --> 00:10:13.342
But what about its sequel,

00:10:13.396 --> 00:10:15.790
Insidious: The Last key?

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.486
Well, I actually did that video five years ago when the movie came out, and

00:10:19.508 --> 00:10:22.654
it actually still holds up pretty decently if you can deal with 24 year old

00:10:22.692 --> 00:10:24.766
me talking like a creepy pasta narrator the whole time.

00:10:24.788 --> 00:10:28.006
Then on the left for you to check out, go in the comments and pay your

00:10:28.028 --> 00:10:29.250
respects to Baby CZ.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:32.774
And if you want to see my analysis of Insidious Five, which is almost here,

00:10:32.812 --> 00:10:35.990
then make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.390
Ring the Deathbell for all notifications.

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.294
Yep, just like that.

00:10:40.332 --> 00:10:43.910
And I will see you in the next one, assuming we both survive.

